SUSPECTED BUG: same Target as save_join_nil_operand with -tags durable (flush is the
f.Sync variant). Expected: the os.Create origin under "source: create: %w", and under
errors.Join the union of the (*os.File).Write origins (seal_write_call_site), the Sync
origins (flush_call_site_durable, with the extra link fmt.Errorf "source: sync: %w") and
the Close origins; a few dozen entries and no Unresolved(fixpoint-limit). Actual: an
"unresolved(fixpoint-limit): result 0 of source.Save can carry more than 1024 values"
entry and a cut listing: the Write operand's io.ErrUnexpectedEOF, the opaque "waiting
for unsupported file type" and the *fs.PathError-wrapped poll.ErrDeadlineExceeded /
ErrNotPollable are missing. The three operand sets of errors.Join are multiplied
(22 x 17 x 8 combinations) and cut at 1024; the marker only appears because the
os.Create value pushes the result over the per-result cap (see
seal_join_silent_truncation for the same cut without any marker).
